# How one environment's traffic is split. Imported by the VPS Caddyfile, the local stack and the
# edge test, so all three route identically. Usage: import routes <prefix>, where the containers
# answer as <prefix>-api and <prefix>-web.
#
# A deploy swaps containers behind each name, so a dial can briefly fail or find no container.
# Caddy retries a failed dial for any method, but re-sends after a failed round trip only for GET,
# so a write is never sent twice.
(routes) {
	@api path /api /api/* /healthz /readyz
	handle @api {
		reverse_proxy {args[0]}-api:8080 {
			lb_try_duration 10s
			lb_try_interval 250ms
		}
	}
	handle {
		reverse_proxy {args[0]}-web:8080 {
			lb_try_duration 10s
			lb_try_interval 250ms
		}
	}
}
